uptime - how long the machine has been up

SYNOPSIS
    uptime

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the time of day, how long since boot, and the load average.

    The load average is how many tasks wanted to run, sampled every five
    seconds and decayed towards each sample over one, five and fifteen
    minutes - the same windows and the same decay constants every other
    UNIX uses, so the numbers mean what they mean elsewhere.

    Also in /proc/loadavg, which is where this reads them from the kernel.

SEE ALSO
    ps, date
